Found under k316 (infra worker, 2026-10-31): OCP::Rex::run_task saves REX_PRIVATE_KEY, REX_PUBLIC_KEY, REX_TASK_PARAMS, OCP_KNOWN_HOSTS and (since k316) PERL5LIB, sets them for the rex child, and restores them after IPC::Run::run returns. If run dies (spawn failure, a timeout that throws), nothing is restored: the next run_task, or anything else in the process, sees the previous task's params and key paths and the prepended lib/.

Fix: `local $ENV{...}` for each (or one guard object), so a die restores them too. Test: a run that dies leaves %ENV as it was.

Note from the same review (no fix asked): if OCP is ever installed into a shared site_perl instead of the image, k316's prepended lib/ is that site_perl and could hide a local::lib's modules from the rex child. In the image and a checkout lib/ holds only OCP.

